[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254636726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3254636726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3254636726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7B_dC2","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T17:05:38Z","updated_at":"2025-09-13T17:05:23Z","body":"You need to add the entries to the expected file, see [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/handling_compatibility_breakages.html) ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254636726/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255878315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3255878315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3255878315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CEMKr","user":{"login":"Giganzo","id":158825920,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXd9wA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158825920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo","html_url":"https://github.com/Giganzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T21:51:16Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T21:52:11Z","body":"I was working on a similar thing. \r\n\r\nThis would not make it possible to show the focus stylebox on grab focus with mouse anymore? \r\nIf yes this could be bad for accessibility and customizing how you want the behavior to work in your game/app.\r\n\r\nW3 has this [note](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/focus-visible.html):\r\n\r\n> There may be situations where mouse/pointer users could also benefit from having a visible focus indicator, even though they did not set focus to an element using the keyboard. As a best practice, consider still providing an explicit focus indicator for these cases.\r\n\r\nAnd I did see a couple of comments when looking into this that says that don't think that a users that need a focus indicator only use keyboard all the time, they might use a mouse in some cases and still need the help of a focus indicator. Say you want an accessibility setting in your game that always draw focus, would this be possible with this PR?\r\n\r\n\r\nAnd how does this handle cases like LineEdit focus? In a browser they get a focus ring even if clicked with a mouse.\r\n\r\nDoes this also include touch input as \"mouse\"?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3255878315/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256006876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3256006876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3256006876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CErjc","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T22:21:11Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T19:46:08Z","body":"> Say you want an accessibility setting in your game that always draw focus, would this be possible with this PR?\r\n\r\n~Currently no, but I'm fine in adding a project setting that forces focus to always show.~\r\nYes, see below.\r\n\r\n> And how does this handle cases like LineEdit focus? In a browser they get a focus ring even if clicked with a mouse.\r\n\r\nNo `Control` gets visible focus via mouse, but I'm open to feedback in changing this in a case-by-case manner.\r\n\r\n> Does this also include touch input as \"mouse\"?\r\n\r\nYes.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3256006876/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3259560914","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3259560914","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3259560914,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CSPPS","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T19:45:51Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T19:45:51Z","body":"I've added `gui/common/always_show_focus_state` to the project settings, disabled by default and tagged as advanced. If set to `true`, it will mimic the old behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3259560914/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260514654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3260514654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3260514654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CV4Fe","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-06T04:20:53Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T04:20:53Z","body":"Did a quick test, mostly works as expected\r\n\r\nHere are some things that still draw focus on mouse input:\r\n\r\n- Filesystem tree when you right click on a file\r\n- Inspector scroll container when you click on a float property (in both inspector dock and project settings)\r\n- Scene tree when you add a new node\r\n\r\nThere are some things that will need to be decided case-by-case, for example popup windows drawing focus after being called is generally good, especially when you're expected to type some text in, or to press a button in a simple yes/no confirmation popup. But some popups however draw focus around the main big area (i.e file selection popup) which most apps don't do because it'd be too visually intrusive. Blender is one example of that, it highlights the buttons in yes/no popups but doesn't highlight the main area of the file selection window even though that's what reacts to keyboard shortcuts\r\n\r\n> I've added `gui/common/always_show_focus_state` to the project settings\r\n\r\nIt currently also affects the editor and not just the game, which will be undesirable if more than one person is working on the project with different preferences on that","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3260514654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3266957448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3266957448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3266957448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CudCI","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-08T15:55:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-08T15:55:46Z","body":"Pointed issues fixed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3266957448/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272240023","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3272240023","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3272240023,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DCmuX","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-09T20:56:31Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T20:56:58Z","body":"When clicking a visibly focused Button, the focus becomes invisible. I tested with [W3 demo](https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_button_test) and the focus stays visible there. So I guess the Godot's behavior should be the same? idk if we want to follow that exactly. If we do, LineEdit should always have visible focus, as already mentioned.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure about hiding focus in the editor. The focus outline helps to know which element is currently active, which is very relevant for shortcuts and other input. Also there are inconsistencies, like 2D/3D viewports having visible focus on mouse enter.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272240023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272417185","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3272417185","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3272417185,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DDR-h","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-09T22:00:54Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T22:00:54Z","body":"> When clicking a visibly focused Button, the focus becomes invisible. I tested with [W3 demo](https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_button_test) and the focus stays visible there. So I guess the Godot's behavior should be the same? idk if we want to follow that exactly. If we do, LineEdit should always have visible focus, as already mentioned.\r\n\r\nI discussed this with Yeldham last week; he said it's intentional to better separate mouse and keyboard focus. I'm not 100% sure the browser behavior is better UX here, so I think it's fine to leave as-is, especially if it makes the implementation simpler. We can revisit this later on if there's a strong need to change it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3272417185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3274986086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250#issuecomment-3274986086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110250","id":3274986086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DNFJm","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","fo